# =========================
# Project gallery images (temporary local placeholders)
# Each project's full image set lives in apps/web/public/projects/<slug>/ for
# now, scraped from Behance ahead of the real CMS/Cloudflare-backed asset API.
# They're heavy (hundreds of MB) and disposable, so they stay untracked -
# every dev who needs them locally re-runs the import rather than everyone
# carrying them in git history forever. The single curated hero image per
# project (public/projects/image-<slug>.png) is unaffected and stays tracked.
# A slash in the middle of a gitignore pattern anchors it to this file's own
# directory (repo root) instead of matching at any depth - that's exactly
# what broke this rule when the app moved into apps/web/, so it's spelled
# out with the full path now rather than assuming it travels on its own.
# =========================
apps/web/public/projects/*/

# Stray copy of the gallery images at the repo root. Nothing serves from
# here (the app reads apps/web/public/), so keep it out of git entirely.
/public/
